Level 9 rule 100230 (Repeated long domain name with TXT/NULL record type) also triggered its parent rule 100214 (TXT/NULL record type). The response for those queries resolved to NXDOMAIN which triggered rule 100220 (Repeated NXdomain). While I can just query for A/AAAA DNS records to blend in with normal traffic, NULL type is almost never seen on live network and TXT records are commonly abused by DNS tunneling tools because they can carry arbitrary text data, making them suitable for command-and-control communication or data transfer.
